{"id":3510,"date":"2021-11-11T06:11:23","date_gmt":"2021-11-11T14:11:23","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3510"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:35:40","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:35:40","slug":"1-6-master-level-1-badge-challenge","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-6-master-level-1-badge-challenge\/","title":{"rendered":"1.6: Master Level 1 Badge Challenge"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22144182428\" name=\"6a22144182428\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Getting Started<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To demonstrate your understanding of python and the CoDrone Mini, you will create a project that addresses one of the following scenarios:<\/p>\n<p>Scenario 1: <span style=\"font-weight: 400\">The space agency is planning a new mission to Mars and they need a drone pilot! They are still in the planning stages of the mission, but they are looking for eager pilots to come up with a sample mission and present it to Mission Control.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>Scenario 2: <span style=\"font-weight: 400\">A wildlife conservation organization heard that drones are great for observing animals in their natural habitats, especially since they can travel farther than humans and see more from the air. They are still in the planning stages of the mission, but they are looking for eager pilots to come up with a sample mission. You pick the animal!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>To get started:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Choose\u00a0 a scenario<\/li>\n<li>Come up with a story for your mission.\n<ol>\n<li>What will be the goal of the mission?<\/li>\n<li>What will the drone need to do to complete the mission?<\/li>\n<li>What value will this mission provide in relationship to the scenario you selected?<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/li>\n<li>Determine what your mission will look like and write or type the steps that your drone will follow.<\/li>\n<li>Make sure your mission meets the requirements listed below:<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2>Mission Requirements<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Includes at least one of each:<\/span>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> takeoff<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> hover<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">land<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Include <\/span><b>at least one<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> positive<strong> AND<\/strong> negative movement in each direction: <\/span>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">roll<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">pitch<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">yaw<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">throttle<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Execute <\/span><b>two<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> flight movements that move in two directions (ex. Roll + pitch)<\/span>\n<ul>\n<li>This can be done through the go() function or with two separate functions<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">There should be <\/span><b>two<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> locations where the drone lands temporarily before continuing<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Flight time (off the ground) should be approximately 90 seconds total<\/span><\/li>\n<li>Includes at least\u00a0<strong>six<\/strong> comments that make the program easier to understand and read<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22144182587\" name=\"6a22144182587\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Writing the Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Now that you have the mission requirements met and you have the steps your drone will complete, write the program. Make sure that you build your program in small parts. Do not try to write everything at once, instead break the program down into small steps and complete each step successfully before moving to the next.<\/p>\n<p>Keep in mind the style and syntax discussed in the lessons. Your program should meet all style and syntax requirements for Python programs in order to be considered correct for this project.<\/p>\n<p>During the process of writing your code, you must also demonstrate how to perform an emergency stop to your instructor.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22144182605\" name=\"6a22144182605\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Presenting Your Results<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Once you have completed your program and met all the flight requirements, you will need to create a presentation in the software of your choice that includes the following information:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Which scenario did you choose<\/li>\n<li>What was the goal of your mission<\/li>\n<li>What value did the mission provide based on the scenario you chose<\/li>\n<li>A description of the steps your drone took to complete the mission including explanations of variables and values used for each step<\/li>\n<li>What trim values did you set and what was the purpose of those trim values<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221441826f2\" name=\"6a221441826f2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Project Requirements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Once you have completed all of the above steps and your instructor has verified that you have met the requirements below, you will be awarded the CoDrone Mini Master Level 1 Badge. Congratulations!<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Students should be able to explain any libraries they are importing and their purpose<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Demonstrate proper Python syntax<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Students should demonstrate how to emergency stop while in autonomous flight.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Set trim values for their drone and explain the purpose<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Includes at least one takeoff, hover, and land<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Include <\/span><b>at least one<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> positive AND negative movement in each direction: roll, pitch, yaw, and throttle<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Execute <\/span><b>two<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> flight movements that move in two directions (ex. Roll + pitch)<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Include at least 1 flight sequence<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Explain what the power and duration parameters are and use at least 3 different values for each throughout their program (For example, they would not be able to use 1 second duration for every single block in their program)<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">There should be <\/span><b>two<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400\"> flight landing pads that they land on somewhere during their flight sequence.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Flight time (off the ground) should be 90 seconds total<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 5 Getting Started [vc_column_text]To demonstrate your understanding of python and the CoDrone Mini, you will create a project that addresses one of the following scenarios: Scenario 1: The&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-6-master-level-1-badge-challenge\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2541,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3473,"_lesson_preview":""},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[],"class_list":["post-3510","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","module-level-1","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3510","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3510\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4173,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3510\/revisions\/4173"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2541"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3510"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-